        "7": {
          "id": "7",
          "name": "sounds.js",
          "contents": "const soundData = {\n  'sound-error-1.wav': { type: 'audio/wav', data: '' },\n  'sound-error-2.wav': { type: 'audio/wav', data: '' },\n  'sound-error-3.wav': { type: 'audio/wav', data: '' },\n  'sound-win.wav': { type: 'audio/wav', data: '' }\n};\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "8": {
          "id": "8",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>4-Square = 4 Times the Fun</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  <script src=\"sounds.js\" defer></script>\n  <script src=\"script.js\" defer></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"app\">\n    <header class=\"app-header\">\n      <h1 class=\"app-title\">4-Square = 4 Times the Fun</h1>\n    </header>\n\n    <noscript><p class=\"notice\">This app needs JavaScript to run.</p></noscript>\n    <p id=\"app-error\" class=\"notice\" hidden>Something went wrong loading this app. Please refresh the page.</p>\n\n    <section id=\"screen-home\" class=\"screen\" aria-labelledby=\"home-heading\">\n      <h2 id=\"home-heading\" tabindex=\"-1\">New to 4-square?</h2>\n      <p>Have you wanted to learn how to play the fun, social game of 4-square, but didn't know where to start? This is the app for you!</p>\n      <img class=\"feature-image\" src=\"four-square.jpg\" width=\"558\" height=\"500\" alt=\"A drawing of a 4-square court with the boxes numbered 1 to 4 and a ball bouncing in box 1\">\n      <div class=\"screen-actions\">\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"primary-button\" data-go=\"screen-players\">More Info</button>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"screen-players\" class=\"screen\" aria-labelledby=\"players-heading\" hidden>\n      <h2 id=\"players-heading\" tabindex=\"-1\">How many players do you need to play 4-Square?</h2>\n      <p>Click to find out!</p>\n\n      <div class=\"count-row\" role=\"group\" aria-labelledby=\"players-heading\">\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"count-button count-one\" data-sound=\"sound-error-1.wav\" data-message=\"Not enough\" aria-label=\"1 player\">1</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"count-button count-two\" data-sound=\"sound-error-2.wav\" data-message=\"Not enough\" aria-label=\"2 players\">2</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"count-button count-three\" data-sound=\"sound-error-3.wav\" data-message=\"Not enough\" aria-label=\"3 players\">3</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"count-button count-four\" data-sound=\"sound-win.wav\" data-message=\"Right! You need four players.\" data-correct=\"true\" aria-label=\"4 players\">4</button>\n      </div>\n      <img class=\"people-image\" src=\"people.jpg\" width=\"2068\" height=\"500\" alt=\"Stick figures showing one player, two players, three players, and four players\">\n\n      <p id=\"answer\" class=\"answer\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">???</p>\n\n      <div class=\"screen-actions\">\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"primary-button\" data-go=\"screen-instructions\">More Info</button>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"screen-instructions\" class=\"screen\" aria-labelledby=\"instructions-heading\" hidden>\n      <h2 id=\"instructions-heading\" tabindex=\"-1\">How to play</h2>\n      <p>To play 4-square, each player stands near one of the four marked boxes on the ground. The boxes are ordered from 1 to 4, with one being the \"top\" box. The player in the 1 box starts play by bouncing the ball in their square and then slapping or hitting the ball into another square. The ball must not touch the original players box again after the initial bounce.</p>\n      <p>If the ball bounces in a player's square, they must then hit the ball into another square before the ball bounces again. They may only hit the ball once. But what if it hits the line, you might ask? There are many different rules on what to do if the ball hits the line - you must agree with your friends if the lines are in or out.</p>\n      <p>If you hit the ball out of bounds or it bounces twice in your square you are out. Everyone moves to the next highest box available (the goal is to stay in the first box as long as possible). If you are out, you go to the back of the line and a new player takes the empty spot in box 4.</p>\n      <img class=\"feature-image\" src=\"rules.jpg\" width=\"910\" height=\"500\" alt=\"Three drawings of a 4-square court: a ball bouncing in box 1, a player in box 2 marked out, and a new player entering box 4 while the others move up\">\n      <div class=\"screen-actions\">\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"primary-button\" data-go=\"screen-home\">Start Again</button>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "9": {
          "id": "9",
          "name": "script.js",
          "contents": "const byId = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\n\nconst soundUrls = {};\n\nfunction getSoundUrl(name) {\n  if (!soundUrls[name]) {\n    const sound = soundData[name];\n    const bytes = Uint8Array.from(atob(sound.data), (character) => character.charCodeAt(0));\n    soundUrls[name] = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([bytes], { type: sound.type }));\n  }\n  return soundUrls[name];\n}\n\nfunction playSound(button) {\n  if (!button.dataset.sound) {\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    const playback = new Audio(getSoundUrl(button.dataset.sound)).play();\n    if (playback && typeof playback.catch === 'function') {\n      playback.catch(() => {});\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    // Sound is optional: the text on screen carries the same feedback.\n  }\n}\n\nfunction showScreen(screenId) {\n  document.querySelectorAll('.screen').forEach((screen) => {\n    screen.hidden = screen.id !== screenId;\n  });\n  window.scrollTo(0, 0);\n  byId(screenId).querySelector('h2').focus();\n}\n\nfunction showAnswer(button) {\n  const answer = byId('answer');\n  const isCorrect = button.dataset.correct === 'true';\n  answer.textContent = button.dataset.message;\n  answer.classList.toggle('is-right', isCorrect);\n  answer.classList.toggle('is-wrong', !isCorrect);\n  playSound(button);\n}\n\nfunction init() {\n  document.querySelectorAll('[data-go]').forEach((button) => {\n    button.addEventListener('click', () => showScreen(button.dataset.go));\n  });\n  document.querySelectorAll('.count-button').forEach((button) => {\n    button.addEventListener('click', () => showAnswer(button));\n  });\n}\n\ntry {\n  init();\n} catch (error) {\n  byId('app-error').hidden = false;\n  document.querySelectorAll('.screen').forEach((screen) => {\n    screen.hidden = true;\n  });\n}\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "7",
        "8",
        "9"
      ]
    },
    "long_instructions": "### Do This\r\n\r\nWith a partner, explore the app. Try every button and picture you can find. Then discuss:\r\n\r\n- How does the user interact with the app?\r\n- What is the purpose of this app?\r\n- Who is the target audience?"
  },
